    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Education",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S4804\n\n TITLE OF BILL :  An act to authorize the Bolivar-Richburg central\nschool district to repay certain excess state aid over a period of 3\nyears\n\n PURPOSE :  This bill adjusts certain state aid payments to the\nBolivar-Richburg central school district so that a $311,962 state aid\noverpayment may be deducted from future state aid payments made to\nsuch school district.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :  This bill allows for deductions from state\naid payments due to the school in the years 2009, 2010, and 2011. Each\ndeduction shall be to the sum of one-third the total of the excess\npayment ($311,962).  There shall be no interest penalty assessed\nagainst the district or collected by the state.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :  Requiring the Bolivar-Richburg school district to\nmake payment directly back to the school in one collective sum would\nplace extreme fiscal strain upon the district. By allowing repayment\nfrom the school's future state aid payments over the next three years,\nthe school will be able to shoulder this financial burden in a more\nappropriate manner and, thereby, allow the school to maintain its\nstandards of educational quality.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY : This is a new bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :  State aid in the amount of $311,962 is to be\nrepaid to the state by deductions made from future state aid payments\nto the school district.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :  Immediately.\n",
